    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The principal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader state</a>, founded after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in July 1099.</li><li>A small Frankish elite ruled a mostly Muslim and Eastern Christian population, relying on castles, military orders and Italian fleets.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>’s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> in 1187 broke it; the kingdom survived on the coast until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluks</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> in 1291.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The kingdom minted gold coins imitating Fatimid dinars, with Arabic inscriptions; after papal objections in the 1250s they carried Christian texts in Arabic.</p></aside>
    </section>

